  "verbalization": "Itoside A appears to have a direct target relationship with Phosphodiesterase 6C, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Pronuciferine, Vitetrifolin B, and Diethylene glycol monolaurate. All of these compounds share a common downstream effect: targeting SNU1. This suggests a potential pathway where Itoside A may influence SNU1 through the activation of Phosphodiesterase 6C, possibly by modulating enzyme activity or signaling pathways. The evidence indicates a consistent link between Itoside A and SNU1 via a shared target, Phosphodiesterase 6C, and the presence of multiple compounds with similar target relationships. The mechanism likely involves the regulation of SNU1 through the phosphodiesterase 6C pathway, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
